## How it works
- Register: the data is validated (email must be unique, password at
  least 8 characters and confirmed). The password is saved with Hash::make().
- Login: Auth::attempt() checks the email and password. If it is correct,
  the session is regenerated and the user goes to the dashboard.
- Dashboard: it uses the auth middleware, so a logged-out user is sent
  to the login page.
- Logout: the session is invalidated and the user goes back to login.

## Answers
1. Hash::make() is used so the password is not saved as plain text.
2. The auth middleware checks if the user is logged in. If not, it
   redirects to the login page.
3. @csrf adds a hidden token to the form to protect it from fake requests.

